// Package place is function-placement filler for the native backends: options
// that randomize where each function lands in .text, as a measurement aid.
// Timing a program over many seeds separates the effect of a code change from
// the effect of the addresses it happens to move; a probe moves one function
// through the phases while the rest of .text stays put, which measures what that
// function's own placement does.  This package holds the options, the hash that
// keys them and the fill arithmetic; common.EmitObject applies them through
// ArchEmitter.PlaceUnit / EmitPlaceFill.  The formulas are specified exactly so
// that tools outside the compiler can reproduce every placement.
package "pkg/binate/native/place"

// PLACE_SPAN is the byte period function placement works modulo: the fill before
// a function is below it, the fills around a probed function total exactly it, and
// phase mode and a probe place a function entry at a chosen offset modulo it.  64
// bytes is the cache-line size of common x86-64 and Arm cores.
const PLACE_SPAN int = 64

// PLACE_SHIFT selects shift mode: before each function, PlaceHash(seed, sym)
// picks a filler length, so a function's address moves by the sum of the fills
// before it, as an unrelated code-size change would move it.
const PLACE_SHIFT int = 0

// PLACE_PHASE selects phase mode (bnc's default): PlaceHash(seed, sym) picks the
// offset modulo PLACE_SPAN of each function's first entry point, and the filler
// before the function is what reaches that offset.  A function's entry phase then
// depends only on the seed and its own symbol, not on the size of the code before
// it.
const PLACE_PHASE int = 1

// PLACE_SEED_MAX is the largest placement seed.  Seeds stay within 31 bits so a
// seed means the same placement on every host, ILP32 included.
const PLACE_SEED_MAX int = 0x7FFFFFFF

// PLACE_FILL_IMM is the immediate of the aarch64 BRK and arm32 BKPT filler
// instructions, so a disassembly tells filler apart from the backend's own traps.
const PLACE_FILL_IMM int = 0x5EED

// PlaceOptions randomizes where each function lands in .text.  The zero value is
// off and leaves the output unchanged byte for byte.  Seed (0..PLACE_SEED_MAX,
// 0 = off) keys the filler; Mode is PLACE_SHIFT or PLACE_PHASE.  Filler is made of
// trap instructions and goes only before Binate functions, after the previous
// function's code (and that function's own trailing filler when it is the probed
// one, below), and right after the probed function.  The hash key of a function is
// its mangled symbol without an object-format prefix, but what the fill positions
// is the function's FIRST entry point: its first #[c_export] alias when it has one
// (a C-entry normalization may then sit between the alias and the mangled symbol),
// the mangled symbol otherwise.
//
// In phase mode EmitObject also aligns .text to PLACE_SPAN, so an offset's phase
// in the object is its phase in the linked program.  A Mach-O object divides into
// per-symbol atoms (MH_SUBSECTIONS_VIA_SYMBOLS) and bnc links Mach-O with
// -dead_strip, so the filler before an object's first function (and the filler
// after any function the link strips) may be discarded.  Phase mode then holds
// only if the linker keeps each atom's offset modulo PLACE_SPAN; ld64.lld does
// not (it aligns an atom only to the largest power of two dividing its offset),
// so after a stripped atom the functions that follow can move off their phase.
// In shift mode a Mach-O function's address need not move by exactly the fills
// before it.
//
// ProbeSym, when not empty, names one function to probe, by the same key as the
// hash (its mangled symbol without an object-format prefix).  At any seed, seed 0
// included, and in either mode, its first entry point lands at offset ProbePhase
// modulo PLACE_SPAN: ProbePhase is a target phase, not a shift, and the filler
// before the function is the one phase mode would emit to reach it.  After the
// function comes PLACE_SPAN minus that filler, so the filler around it always
// totals PLACE_SPAN and every later byte of .text lands at the same offset for
// every ProbePhase, phase 0 included: timing a program over the probe phases
// measures the phase of that one function.  (Only what refers to the probed
// function itself, such as a call's displacement, changes with the phase.)
// Other functions get the filler Seed and Mode give them, none at seed 0.
// ProbePhase is a multiple of the filler unit in 0..PLACE_SPAN-1, and 0 without a
// probe.  With a probe EmitObject aligns .text to PLACE_SPAN in either mode.  A
// probe that names no function of a module changes nothing in its object but that
// alignment; one object sees one module, so only a tool that reads the linked
// program can tell that a probe matched nothing.
type PlaceOptions struct {
	Seed       int
	Mode       int
	ProbeSym   @[]char
	ProbePhase int
}

// PlaceActive reports whether p adds any filler: a nonzero seed or a probe.
func PlaceActive(p PlaceOptions) bool

// PlaceHash is the placement hash of a symbol under a seed.  All arithmetic is on
// uint32 and wraps modulo 2^32: h = FNV-1a-32 of key's bytes (h = 0x811C9DC5,
// then per byte h = (h ^ byte) * 0x01000193); h ^= uint32(seed) * 0x9E3779B9;
// then murmur3's fmix32 (h ^= h >> 16; h *= 0x85EBCA6B; h ^= h >> 13;
// h *= 0xC2B2AE35; h ^= h >> 16).
func PlaceHash(seed int, key *[]readonly char) uint32

// PlaceFillBefore returns the filler bytes to emit before the function whose
// mangled symbol (without an object-format prefix) is sym, when the current .text
// offset is off and the filler granularity is unit.  With K = PLACE_SPAN / unit
// and idx = PlaceHash(p.Seed, sym) mod K: shift mode returns unit * idx; phase
// mode returns the fill that moves alignUp(off, unit) to unit * idx modulo
// PLACE_SPAN.  For the probe symbol (p.ProbeSym), in either mode and at any seed,
// it returns the fill that moves alignUp(off, unit) to p.ProbePhase modulo
// PLACE_SPAN.  0 for any other function at seed 0.  p and unit must pass
// PlaceCheck.
//
// Phase mode is exact only if the function's first entry point lands at
// alignUp(off, unit) + fill: the backend must emit nothing else between the fill
// and the entry, and either align the entry to exactly unit or keep every .text
// offset a multiple of unit (then no alignment is needed).
func PlaceFillBefore(p PlaceOptions, sym *[]readonly char, unit int, off int) int

// PlaceFillAfter returns the filler bytes to emit right after the function whose
// mangled symbol is sym, given that PlaceFillBefore put before bytes in front of
// it: PLACE_SPAN - before for the probe symbol, 0 for every other function.  So
// the probed function's filler totals PLACE_SPAN whatever its phase.
func PlaceFillAfter(p PlaceOptions, sym *[]readonly char, before int) int

// PlaceCheck validates p for filler granularity unit: "" when valid, otherwise
// the reason (a seed outside 0..PLACE_SEED_MAX, an unknown mode, a unit that is
// not a positive divisor of PLACE_SPAN, a probe phase that is not a multiple of
// unit in 0..PLACE_SPAN-1, or a nonzero probe phase without a probe symbol).
func PlaceCheck(p PlaceOptions, unit int) @[]readonly char
